  "lines": [
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "Think about the software you trust most on your computer.",
      "emphasis": "software",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "TRUSTED TOOL",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "If you write code, there's a good chance it's your code editor.",
      "emphasis": "there's",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "door",
        "key"
      ],
      "label": "ENTRY POINT",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "It sees your files, your projects, your passwords sitting in config files.",
      "emphasis": "passwords",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "door",
        "key"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "And that's exactly why attackers want to get inside it.",
      "emphasis": "attackers",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "marketplace",
        "extension"
      ],
      "label": "LOOKS SAFE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "Picture an extension that looks completely normal in the marketplace.",
      "emphasis": "marketplace",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "file",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "FIRST ACCESS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "You install it like you've installed a hundred others.",
      "emphasis": "installed",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "door"
      ],
      "label": "PERSISTENCE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "But in the background, it reads your files, talks to a server somewhere,",
      "emphasis": "background",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "desk"
      ],
      "label": "YOUR MACHINE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "and leaves a door open that stays open even after you remove it.",
      "emphasis": "leaves",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "desk"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "That's not a movie plot.",
      "emphasis": "That's",
      "visual": "clock",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "clock"
      ],
      "label": "RECENT CASE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "It starts with software you invited in yourself,",
      "emphasis": "software",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "warning"
      ],
      "label": "REAL RISK",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "cta",
      "text": "and what just happened with Cursor shows how fast that invitation can go wrong.",
      "emphasis": "invitation",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "phone"
      ],
      "label": "FOLLOW",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "If you like tech explained in plain English like this, follow the channel.",
      "emphasis": "explained",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "checkmark"
      ],
      "label": "LOOKS USEFUL",
      "follow": true
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "Because the real question here isn't whether an extension looks useful.",
      "emphasis": "extension",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "checkmark"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 0,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "It's what it can do once your editor trusts it.",
      "emphasis": "editor",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "editor",
        "key",
        "computer"
      ],
      "label": "REAL QUESTION",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "So what actually happened?",
      "emphasis": "happened",
      "visual": "clock",
      "subjects": [
        "calendar",
        "marketplace"
      ],
      "label": "OCTOBER 29",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "On October 29th, 2026, Cursor reported a problem in its extension marketplace.",
      "emphasis": "October",
      "visual": "bar_chart",
      "subjects": [
        "version labels",
        "marketplace"
      ],
      "label": "TWO VERSIONS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "Versions 2.1.312 and 2.1.313 of a Claude Code extension, branded with Anthropic's name,",
      "emphasis": "Anthropic's",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "extension"
      ],
      "label": "FAMILIAR NAME",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "turned out to be malicious copies.",
      "emphasis": "malicious",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "extension"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "Cursor said they came through its own VS Code Extension Marketplace,",
      "emphasis": "Marketplace",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "marketplace",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "DISTRIBUTION",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "and they weren't real Anthropic builds.",
      "emphasis": "Anthropic",
      "visual": "split_compare",
      "subjects": [
        "marketplace",
        "factory"
      ],
      "label": "WHO BUILT IT",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "And that part matters.",
      "emphasis": "matters",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "logo",
        "extension"
      ],
      "label": "FAMILIAR LABEL",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "The name looked familiar,",
      "emphasis": "familiar",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "marketplace",
        "package",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "DELIVERY ROUTE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "and the marketplace felt like a safe place to get it,",
      "emphasis": "marketplace",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "marketplace",
        "package",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "so nobody had to download anything that looked like a virus.",
      "emphasis": "download",
      "visual": "cross_out",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "virus"
      ],
      "label": "NO OBVIOUS FILE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "The dangerous code came in through a perfectly ordinary install.",
      "emphasis": "dangerous",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "button",
        "extension",
        "computer"
      ],
      "label": "ONE INSTALL",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "Microsoft looked at the tampered extension and found JavaScript injected into it.",
      "emphasis": "JavaScript",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "code window"
      ],
      "label": "INJECTED CODE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "That code tried to add an SSH key controlled by the attacker,",
      "emphasis": "controlled",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "key",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "NEW KEY",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "set up a reverse SSH tunnel that would keep running,",
      "emphasis": "reverse",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "tunnel",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "OPEN TUNNEL",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "and collect information about the machine.",
      "emphasis": "information",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "tunnel",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "Now, an SSH key is basically a spare key to your computer.",
      "emphasis": "basically",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "tunnel",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "And a reverse tunnel is a way for",
      "emphasis": "reverse",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "key",
        "house"
      ],
      "label": "SPARE KEY",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "an outside computer to call back into yours.",
      "emphasis": "computer",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "server",
        "tunnel",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "CALL BACK",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "The clever bit is that your own machine opens",
      "emphasis": "machine",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "tunnel",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "STAYING OPEN",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "that connection by reaching out to the attacker's server,",
      "emphasis": "connection",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "network",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "OUTBOUND PATH",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "so it can keep working quietly.",
      "emphasis": "working",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "network",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "Cursor also warned that just uninstalling the extension might not be enough,",
      "emphasis": "uninstalling",
      "visual": "cross_out",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "trash bin",
        "door"
      ],
      "label": "UNINSTALLING",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "because it could leave changes elsewhere on the system.",
      "emphasis": "elsewhere",
      "visual": "icon_orbit",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "key",
        "folder",
        "terminal"
      ],
      "label": "BEYOND THE FOLDER",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "That's the whole supply-chain trick, really.",
      "emphasis": "supply-chain",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "badge",
        "package"
      ],
      "label": "BORROWED TRUST",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "You borrow someone else's good name,",
      "emphasis": "someone",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "badge",
        "package",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "ACCEPTED",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "and you use it to deliver something people will happily accept.",
      "emphasis": "something",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "badge",
        "package",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "The marketplace wasn't the final target.",
      "emphasis": "final target",
      "visual": "split_compare",
      "subjects": [
        "marketplace",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "DELIVERY POINT",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "It just had to be the trusted road in.",
      "emphasis": "trusted",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "marketplace",
        "door",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "PATH IN",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "But the extension on its own is only part of the story.",
      "emphasis": "extension",
      "visual": "cross_out",
      "subjects": [
        "editor",
        "button"
      ],
      "label": "MORE THAN UI",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "An extension isn't just a button in your editor.",
      "emphasis": "extension",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "computer",
        "key"
      ],
      "label": "RUNNING CODE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "It's real software, running with the permissions of the extension host.",
      "emphasis": "permissions",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "file",
        "computer"
      ],
      "label": "FILE ACCESS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "VS Code's own documentation says extensions can read and write files, make network requests,",
      "emphasis": "extensions",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "computer",
        "server",
        "terminal"
      ],
      "label": "SYSTEM ACCESS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "start other programs and change settings.",
      "emphasis": "programs",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "checkmark"
      ],
      "label": "LEGITIMATE USE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "That's all great when the code is honest.",
      "emphasis": "That's",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "warning"
      ],
      "label": "MALICIOUS USE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "When the code belongs to an attacker, it's a different picture.",
      "emphasis": "different",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "warning"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "Think about what's sitting in a developer's project files and environment variables.",
      "emphasis": "environment variables",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "folder",
        "file",
        "terminal"
      ],
      "label": "SEARCHING",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "Tokens, configuration, credentials.",
      "emphasis": "credentials",
      "visual": "icon_orbit",
      "subjects": [
        "token",
        "folder",
        "key",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "VALUABLE FILES",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "A token can look like a random line of text,",
      "emphasis": "token",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "text file",
        "key"
      ],
      "label": "HIDDEN VALUE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "but it might be permission to get into another service.",
      "emphasis": "permission",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "key",
        "server",
        "cloud"
      ],
      "label": "REMOTE ACCESS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "So the extension can look through those files,",
      "emphasis": "extension",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "network",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "OUTBOUND",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "reach out to a server without it looking like a download,",
      "emphasis": "download",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "network",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "and send what it finds through the connection it already opened.",
      "emphasis": "connection",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "file",
        "network",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "DATA PATH",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "It can also make sure it survives a restart.",
      "emphasis": "survives",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "restart arrow"
      ],
      "label": "PERSISTENCE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "That's what people mean by persistence.",
      "emphasis": "persistence",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "gear"
      ],
      "label": "STARTUP",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "Maybe it's a startup task, maybe it's a changed setting,",
      "emphasis": "startup",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "key",
        "trash bin"
      ],
      "label": "LEFT BEHIND",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "or an SSH key that stays behind after the extension is gone.",
      "emphasis": "extension",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "boot"
      ],
      "label": "FOOTHOLD",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "And now that laptop is the attacker's foothold.",
      "emphasis": "foothold",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "boot"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "From there, they could go after source code, GitHub tokens, cloud credentials, package registries,",
      "emphasis": "GitHub tokens",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "code",
        "token"
      ],
      "label": "NEXT TARGET",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "signing keys, even production systems.",
      "emphasis": "signing keys",
      "visual": "icon_orbit",
      "subjects": [
        "cloud",
        "registry",
        "key",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "WIDER REACH",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "So a small extension can be the first link in a much bigger chain,",
      "emphasis": "extension",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "laptop",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "CHAIN REACTION",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 2,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "and the first secret it steals might not be what they're really after.",
      "emphasis": "they're",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "key",
        "laptop",
        "cloud"
      ],
      "label": "NEXT STEP",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "And this gets even more serious once you",
      "emphasis": "serious",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "AMPLIFIER",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "add AI coding tools to the picture.",
      "emphasis": "picture",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "folder",
        "code"
      ],
      "label": "READING",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "Cursor describes its agents as tools that search and read your codebase, edit files,",
      "emphasis": "describes",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "terminal",
        "package"
      ],
      "label": "ACTING",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "run terminal commands and install dependencies.",
      "emphasis": "dependencies",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "terminal"
      ],
      "label": "NOT JUST CHAT",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "That's the whole point of an agent.",
      "emphasis": "That's",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "terminal"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "It doesn't just suggest things, it actually does them.",
      "emphasis": "actually",
      "visual": "split_compare",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "person"
      ],
      "label": "SUGGESTION VERSUS ACTION",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "So a compromised extension isn't just sitting next to your AI assistant.",
      "emphasis": "compromised extension",
      "visual": "cross_out",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "robot"
      ],
      "label": "NOT SEPARATE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "It might be in control of the environment the assistant works in.",
      "emphasis": "control",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "computer"
      ],
      "label": "CONTROL",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "There are really 2 risks here, and they overlap.",
      "emphasis": "overlap",
      "visual": "icon_orbit",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "warning",
        "robot"
      ],
      "label": "TWO RISKS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "First, the extension can attack your computer directly.",
      "emphasis": "directly",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "laptop",
        "warning"
      ],
      "label": "DIRECT ATTACK",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "Second, a poisoned project can steer the AI agent.",
      "emphasis": "poisoned",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "repository",
        "robot"
      ],
      "label": "INDIRECT ATTACK",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "A file in the project can carry instructions",
      "emphasis": "instructions",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "repository",
        "robot"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "that the agent reads as normal context,",
      "emphasis": "context",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "repository",
        "robot"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "and the agent might use its legitimate permissions to carry them out.",
      "emphasis": "permissions",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "file",
        "robot",
        "speech bubble"
      ],
      "label": "HIDDEN INSTRUCTIONS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "Researchers showed this working on Cursor and Copilot in tested scenarios.",
      "emphasis": "Researchers",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "key"
      ],
      "label": "REAL PERMISSIONS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "proof",
      "text": "That doesn't mean every session out there is compromised.",
      "emphasis": "compromised",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "research paper",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "RESEARCH",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "The danger is simpler than that.",
      "emphasis": "simpler",
      "visual": "cross_out",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "warning"
      ],
      "label": "IMPORTANT LIMIT",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "The agent doesn't have to understand every instruction.",
      "emphasis": "every instruction",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "file"
      ],
      "label": "NOT OMNISCIENT",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "One instruction that gets through can be enough",
      "emphasis": "instruction",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "file"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "pattern",
      "text": "to make real things happen on your machine.",
      "emphasis": "machine",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "file",
        "robot",
        "terminal"
      ],
      "label": "TRIGGERED ACTION",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "And that's the bigger lesson.",
      "emphasis": "that's",
      "visual": "line_chart",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "network"
      ],
      "label": "AMPLIFIED VALUE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "AI makes every trusted connection in your setup worth more to an attacker.",
      "emphasis": "trusted connection",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "key",
        "server"
      ],
      "label": "CONNECTED SYSTEMS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "So how do you make this safer?",
      "emphasis": "safer",
      "visual": "gauge",
      "subjects": [
        "chain",
        "scale"
      ],
      "label": "THE QUESTION",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "First, the problem isn't that AI is somehow evil.",
      "emphasis": "problem",
      "visual": "cross_out",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "warning"
      ],
      "label": "NOT MAGIC",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "The real issue is permission you can't see",
      "emphasis": "permission",
      "visual": "cross_out",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "warning"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "turning into action that happens on its own.",
      "emphasis": "turning",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "key",
        "robot",
        "terminal"
      ],
      "label": "HIDDEN POWER",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Start by getting extensions from verified sources,",
      "emphasis": "extensions",
      "visual": "checklist",
      "subjects": [
        "marketplace",
        "checkmark"
      ],
      "label": "CHECK SOURCE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "and keep a record of which versions you're running instead of updating blindly.",
      "emphasis": "versions",
      "visual": "checklist",
      "subjects": [
        "version label",
        "notebook"
      ],
      "label": "PIN VERSIONS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Workspace trust and sandboxing can limit what software is able to reach.",
      "emphasis": "sandboxing",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "workspace",
        "sandbox",
        "key"
      ],
      "label": "LIMIT ACCESS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Accounts with only the access they need can",
      "emphasis": "Accounts",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "workspace",
        "sandbox",
        "key"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "limit the damage if one thing gets compromised.",
      "emphasis": "compromised",
      "visual": "gauge",
      "subjects": [
        "account",
        "lock"
      ],
      "label": "SMALLER BLAST",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Keep your secrets out of files an agent can read,",
      "emphasis": "secrets",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "key",
        "file"
      ],
      "label": "HIDE SECRETS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "and make terminal commands and outside tools ask for your approval first.",
      "emphasis": "terminal",
      "visual": "checklist",
      "subjects": [
        "terminal",
        "approval button"
      ],
      "label": "APPROVE ACTIONS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Let me ask you something.",
      "emphasis": "something",
      "visual": "checklist",
      "subjects": [
        "terminal",
        "approval button"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Have you ever installed an extension and only checked its folder inside the editor?",
      "emphasis": "installed",
      "visual": "checklist",
      "subjects": [
        "terminal",
        "approval button"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "That's not enough on its own.",
      "emphasis": "That's",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "folder",
        "gear",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "CHECK AFTERWARD",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "Changes to your startup settings and other system settings",
      "emphasis": "settings",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "folder",
        "editor"
      ],
      "label": "LOOK OUTSIDE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "deserve a look after you install something too.",
      "emphasis": "something",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "isolation barrier"
      ],
      "label": "ISOLATE",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "And if you did install a compromised version, take that machine off the network,",
      "emphasis": "machine",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "isolation barrier"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "cost",
      "text": "then replace every credential it could have reached.",
      "emphasis": "credential",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "key",
        "token",
        "circular arrow"
      ],
      "label": "ROTATE KEYS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "Uninstalling the extension you can see doesn't prove the backdoor is gone,",
      "emphasis": "Uninstalling",
      "visual": "cross_out",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "backdoor"
      ],
      "label": "NOT ENOUGH",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "because what you can see might not be the whole infection.",
      "emphasis": "whole infection",
      "visual": "icon_pair",
      "subjects": [
        "program",
        "hidden door"
      ],
      "label": "LOOK DEEPER",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "Convenience is only safe when you can still",
      "emphasis": "Convenience",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "boundary line",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "VISIBLE BOUNDARY",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "see where the trust starts and stops, keep it narrow,",
      "emphasis": "starts",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "boundary line",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 4,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "and check it yourself before a tool gets that much power.",
      "emphasis": "yourself",
      "visual": "checklist",
      "subjects": [
        "software",
        "lock",
        "checkmark"
      ],
      "label": "CHECK FIRST",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "So put it all together and it comes down to one simple fact.",
      "emphasis": "together",
      "visual": "icon_hero",
      "subjects": [
        "extension",
        "door"
      ],
      "label": "CORE IDEA",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "Your code editor already sits right next to your files,",
      "emphasis": "already",
      "visual": "icon_orbit",
      "subjects": [
        "file",
        "terminal",
        "key"
      ],
      "label": "CLOSE ACCESS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "claim",
      "text": "your terminal and your credentials.",
      "emphasis": "credentials",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "robot",
        "laptop",
        "gear"
      ],
      "label": "AMPLIFIED ACCESS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "AI coding tools take that access and turn it into a workflow.",
      "emphasis": "workflow",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "marketplace",
        "extension",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "THREE LINKS",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "The marketplace gives the trust, the extension gives the access,",
      "emphasis": "access",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "marketplace",
        "extension",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "and the agent turns that access into action.",
      "emphasis": "access",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "marketplace",
        "extension",
        "laptop"
      ],
      "label": "",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "reframe",
      "text": "The answer isn't giving up the convenience.",
      "emphasis": "convenience",
      "visual": "icon_flow",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "robot",
        "terminal"
      ],
      "label": "ACTION CHAIN",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "cta",
      "text": "It's better boundaries,",
      "emphasis": "better boundaries",
      "visual": "split_compare",
      "subjects": [
        "convenience",
        "boundary"
      ],
      "label": "BETTER BOUNDARIES",
      "follow": false
    },
    {
      "chapter": 5,
      "section": "cta",
      "text": "and trusting a tool only as far as you can actually check it.",
      "emphasis": "trusting",
      "visual": "logo_end",
      "subjects": [
        "laptop",
        "checkmark"
      ],
      "label": "VERIFY TRUST",
      "follow": false
    }
  ]
}
